        "original_id": "fa8e80fd-8de7-58e8-ad1d-ac0380688ab9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Earle Leonard Nelson, Keith Hunter Jesperson, Gordon Stewart Northcott, William Dean Christenson\n- Topics: Canadian serial killer definition, Cold North Killers: Canadian Serial Murder\n\nFacts:\n- Cold North Killers: Canadian Serial Murder defines a Canadian serial killer to include Canadians who committed murder abroad.\n- Cold North Killers: Canadian Serial Murder defines a Canadian serial killer to include non-Canadians who committed murder in Canada.\n- Cold North Killers: Canadian Serial Murder gives Keith Hunter Jesperson and Gordon Stewart Northcott as examples of Canadians who committed murder abroad.\n- Cold North Killers: Canadian Serial Murder gives William Dean Christenson and Earle Leonard Nelson as examples of non-Canadians who committed murder in Canada.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson was born on May 12, 1897.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson was known as the Gorilla Man.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson was an American serial killer.\n- Earle Leonard Nelson died on January 13, 1928.",
